1
00:00:02,280 --> 00:00:05,020
Did you say the death lament Stratum?

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:10,195
Yep, we're planning on
accepting a request to go there.

3
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,381
You guys feel like tagging along?

4
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:16,517
Isn't that Stratum filled with creepy
stuff like corpse and skeleton fiends?

5
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:18,937
You're making it sound like
you're going on vacation.

6
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:21,491
Are you really going to a place like that?

7
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:23,227
Yeah, we'll be leaving soon.

8
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:24,230
Are you busy?

9
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,437
Well, no, that's not the issue.

10
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:31,537
Now that I think about it, you were
never good with spooky stuff, Lamas.

11
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:34,480
Is it too scary for you?
What? Obviously not!

12
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,777
Only a child would
still be afraid of that!

13
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:37,690
Hmm.

14
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,536
Ah, you don't like scary things, huh?

15
00:00:40,700 --> 00:00:44,288
It's just a bunch of moving
skeletons, corpses, and ghosties.

16
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:46,377
It's not like there's anything really bad.

17
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:47,872
There's no need to fear.

18
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:51,277
Captain, it's perfectly normal
to be scared of those things.

19
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:56,301
You can't seriously expect everybody you
meet to be as stupidly fearless as you are.

20
00:00:57,660 --> 00:00:59,597
Everything I've heard about that place has

21
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:02,317
been second hand information
could you tell me a

22
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:04,397
little bit more about
the dead's lament stratum

23
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:07,457
what do you want to
know the sky overhead is

24
00:01:07,540 --> 00:01:09,837
covered in thick stormy
clouds with constant

25
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:12,257
flashes of lightning
because of that it always

26
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:14,277
feels chilly and there
are these crumbling and

27
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:17,242
decrepit gravestones
scattered all over the place

28
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:21,920
I didn't know llamas had this much
trouble dealing with scary things

29
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:07,920
I don't know.

30
00:02:32,860 --> 00:02:35,660
Thank you.

31
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:01,677
Hey, Lamas, you're not actually
scared of that kind of stuff, right?

32
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:02,590
Huh?

33
00:03:02,673 --> 00:03:03,780
Well, uh, of course I'm not.

34
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,360
Come on, guys, it's me.

35
00:03:05,540 --> 00:03:06,657
I ain't afraid of no ghosts.

36
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:07,860
That's news to me.

37
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:11,377
I remember how you used to be
when you heard a scary story.

38
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:13,937
You wouldn't even go to
the bathroom by yourself.

39
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:14,850
You, me?

40
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,980
Ugh, don't bring that up.

41
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:18,840
It's ancient history. Well,

42
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:21,897
we're not going to force Lamas to
come with us if she doesn't want to,

43
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:24,297
so the question is, who's
going to carry Boxo?

44
00:03:24,380 --> 00:03:28,900
Nobody in our group has that kind of
strength. What to do? Let's see here.

45
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,897
We were counting on
being able to bring Boxo.

46
00:03:31,980 --> 00:03:36,020
If he's not accompanying us, a
long-term campaign will be hard.

47
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:40,197
I doubt the Stratum Lord there is
going to just stay in one place.

48
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,809
The search for it won't
be a simple matter.

49
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,310
Besides...

50
00:03:45,393 --> 00:03:46,637
Hold on! Don't count me out!

51
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:49,297
I never actually said
I wouldn't go with you.

52
00:03:49,380 --> 00:03:50,851
It'll be fine, I promise.

53
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,420
I can totally handle scary stuff.

54
00:03:53,720 --> 00:03:54,820
How is that so?

55
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:58,417
You should have no problem going
to the Dead's Lament Stratum then.

56
00:03:58,500 --> 00:03:59,560
Yep, no problem.

57
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:01,940
Great, I'm happy to hear that.

58
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:05,100
Okay, we'll head in first.

59
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:09,106
As soon as we get everything
sorted, we'll be right behind you.

60
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:11,057
Oh, Phil Mina's not coming?

61
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,320
Oh, she decided to sit this one out.

62
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:15,997
The vice captain gets
frightened pretty easily.

63
00:04:16,080 --> 00:04:17,240
Yep, yep.

64
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,720
Must be nice for her.

65
00:04:34,400 --> 00:04:35,380
Here we are.

66
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:38,357
This will be our home base for a while.

67
00:04:38,440 --> 00:04:41,617
You're saying we're going to
make a camp in a place like this?

68
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,797
She's such a chicken.

69
00:04:42,880 --> 00:04:44,057
She's practically clucking.

70
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:47,240
If you can't handle it
anymore, just say the word.

71
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:50,877
We'll turn around and go back
to the Clearflow Lake Stratom.

72
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:53,254
Hope you were d-d-d-diculous, I'm fine!

73
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:55,302
You don't have to worry one bit!

74
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:57,681
Alright then, let's check it out!

75
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,220
Ah, there you are. Welcome.

76
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,620
I've been awaiting your arrival.

77
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:16,950
Who?

78
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:21,400
I figured she was lying, but this
is even worse than I expected.

79
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:23,897
Believe it or not, she's handled it well.

80
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:24,810
Trust me.

81
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:29,533
Carrying her to her room won't be a
problem, but what do we do about Boxo?

82
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:35,080
Oh, nice one, Boxo.

83
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:39,988
Madam, do you mind if we get
Boxo set up in front of the inn?

84
00:05:40,540 --> 00:05:41,370
Not at all.

85
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:43,897
This must be the magic item with a mind of

86
00:05:43,980 --> 00:05:46,457
its own that I've heard
so much about recently,

87
00:05:46,540 --> 00:05:47,370
right?

88
00:05:49,020 --> 00:05:49,980
How mysterious.

89
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:53,290
It's funny.

90
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:56,397
So much has changed, but Lamas
is still the same as ever.

91
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:59,617
As soon as you began telling
a scary story just like that,

92
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:02,417
she'd cover her ears and
start screaming bloody murder.

93
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:03,853
It takes me right back.

94
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:08,704
Hulemy likes to tease Lamas, but
it's obvious they're very close.

95
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:11,259
They almost seem more like sisters.

96
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:14,157
Normally, she would have
run back home by now.

97
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:16,711
I guess she can't bear to leave this time.

98
00:06:17,160 --> 00:06:19,397
I hope she's not forcing
herself to stay because

99
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:22,217
she's afraid that there'd
be nobody left to carry me.

100
00:06:22,300 --> 00:06:23,280
By the way,

101
00:06:23,640 --> 00:06:26,277
something tells me you're
misinterpreting the situation,

102
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:30,419
so I might as well tell you the
truth why Lamas is being so stubborn.

103
00:06:30,620 --> 00:06:34,180
Wait, it might hurt her
feelings if I do. Too bad!

104
00:06:35,680 --> 00:06:38,856
Well, I bet you'll figure
it out if you think it over.

105
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:42,610
Hmm?

106
00:06:42,693 --> 00:06:43,523
What could it be?

107
00:06:58,980 --> 00:06:59,810
Huh?

108
00:06:59,893 --> 00:07:00,723
Wait a sec.

109
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:03,740
Those are flame skulls.

110
00:07:06,340 --> 00:07:09,217
But for some reason, they're
just wandering around.

111
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:10,476
What are they doing?

112
00:07:14,860 --> 00:07:17,742
This is kind of like one
of those haunted houses.

113
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,734
I'll play it safe and put up a barrier.

114
00:07:21,540 --> 00:07:26,069
This might be a good chance to see if
any anti-undead remedies actually work.

115
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:28,720
Well, salt is the old standard.

116
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:32,645
Rock salt should do the trick.

117
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:38,290
Nothing, huh?

118
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:41,014
You can't trust the old tails, I guess.

119
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:43,555
Maybe this will work.

120
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,918
This is supposed to be good
for dealing with spirits.

121
00:07:50,860 --> 00:07:51,690
Take that!

122
00:07:53,880 --> 00:07:54,710
Huh?

123
00:07:55,140 --> 00:07:57,081
I really thought that would work.

124
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:59,380
Could it be I need more of them?

125
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:03,300
Morning, Boxo.

126
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,521
Did you get any sleep last night?

127
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:07,240
Where did this come from?

128
00:08:08,800 --> 00:08:10,680
I tried all sorts of things,

129
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:14,626
but none of them had any effect
on these otherworldly monsters.

130
00:08:17,020 --> 00:08:18,897
As soon as Shui and the others arrived,

131
00:08:18,980 --> 00:08:22,777
Captain Kerioyl immediately sent
them out again to survey the area.

132
00:08:22,860 --> 00:08:26,777
The captain mentioned something about
gathering allies to help tackle the stratum,

133
00:08:26,860 --> 00:08:28,566
and then went off on his own.

134
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:34,380
Oh, Mr. Boxxo.

135
00:08:36,960 --> 00:08:40,431
I hope you weren't too surprised
by last night's spectacle.

136
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,014
When did she get here?

137
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:43,592
She came out of nowhere.

138
00:08:44,460 --> 00:08:46,900
In this place, whenever night falls,

139
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:50,517
monsters tend to gather, even
in the middle of the village.

140
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:55,277
Only those who are confident venture out
at night, but not all of them make it back.

141
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:58,301
I kind of wish you had
told me that ahead of time.

142
00:08:58,520 --> 00:09:02,040
You see, the monsters in
this stratum envy the living.

143
00:09:02,540 --> 00:09:05,260
Of course, that means
you're safe from them.

144
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,700
I sincerely doubt they'd attack you.

145
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:10,657
So that's why they pretty
much left me alone.

146
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:13,622
They were just trying to
look into the buildings.

147
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:17,220
You're more akin to them not being alive.

148
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:18,770
Marvelous.

149
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,840
I didn't mean any offense by that.

150
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:23,350
Well,

151
00:09:23,433 --> 00:09:26,357
I'm basically a vending machine being
possessed by the soul of a human,

152
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:28,087
So you're not exactly wrong.

153
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:32,738
That said, I'm not so sure that I'm
more akin to a ghost than you are.

154
00:09:36,420 --> 00:09:38,400
Sorry about yesterday, Boxo.

155
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:40,580
It's my fault. Hello there!

156
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:50,760
I don't know how much longer
I can keep this up. Too bad.

157
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,150
Yeah, you're right.

158
00:09:52,233 --> 00:09:54,880
This is going really bad. Uh-oh.

159
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,357
She's in negative mode.

160
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:58,852
and taking my canned responses literally.

161
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:00,590
Whoa!

162
00:10:00,673 --> 00:10:02,438
Come on, this isn't like you, Lamas.

163
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:05,497
If something's holding you
back, then just overcome it.

164
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:06,992
It's what you always do.

165
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:08,848
Why didn't I think of that?

166
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:12,580
Yeah, all I have to do is
get used to it. Well said.

167
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:16,237
Now, I'm gonna give you a crash
course in beating your fear.

168
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,420
Huh? Crash course?

169
00:10:18,780 --> 00:10:21,040
Right, I mean, thank you, ma 'am.

170
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:25,197
For your first lesson, I'd like you to
take a leisurely stroll around the village.

171
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,720
Wait, by myself?

172
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,280
Nope, no way, lady.

173
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,000
You gave in too quickly.

174
00:10:31,500 --> 00:10:35,817
I get that it's a little gloomy over
there, but it's daytime, so you'll be fine.

175
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:38,297
You say that, but the mood
is different around here.

176
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:40,857
If the Clear Flow Lake
Stratum is a frog fiend,

177
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:43,116
this place is like a king frog fiend.

178
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:46,677
That made no sense, but I kind
of get what she's trying to say.

179
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:47,777
Since you're giving up,

180
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:50,357
does that mean you're going back
to the Clear Flow Lake Stratum?

181
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,381
I'm not leaving.

182
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,537
Then all you can do is
tough it out, right?

183
00:10:53,620 --> 00:10:55,780
I guess you have a point there.

184
00:10:56,920 --> 00:11:00,177
Okay, there's a general store
near the village entrance.

185
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:02,377
I want you to get some
restorative potions.

186
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:04,000
Yeah, fine, I'll go.

187
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:05,780
Come on, Voxo.

188
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:07,606
Let's try to make this quick.

189
00:11:07,760 --> 00:11:10,180
You are going alone. Very funny.

190
00:11:10,340 --> 00:11:11,660
Anyway, I'm serious.

191
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:16,080
No problem, just you watch me.

192
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:18,157
I'll show you I'm not a kid anymore.

193
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,946
This will be a piece of cake.

194
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,060
I can do this.

195
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,277
There's nothing to be afraid of.

196
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,242
I won't falter.

197
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,977
This must be how a parent
feels when they watch

198
00:11:28,060 --> 00:11:31,060
their child go out on their
own for the first time.

199
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,000
It's too scary!

200
00:11:40,920 --> 00:11:41,920
Aw, there, there.

201
00:11:42,020 --> 00:11:43,196
That was a good try.

202
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:46,337
Give me a second and I'll heat
up some corn soup for you.

203
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:48,832
Or maybe something sweet would be better.

204
00:11:49,260 --> 00:11:50,554
Don't coddle the girl.

205
00:11:51,260 --> 00:11:52,160
Sorry, Lamas.

206
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:53,600
I wish I could help.

207
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:59,797
You know, when I think about
it, my job is to carry Boxo,

208
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:02,497
so this training is useless
if I don't have him with me.

209
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:03,600
All right, fine.

210
00:12:03,900 --> 00:12:06,076
If it helps, you can bring him along.

211
00:12:06,380 --> 00:12:07,210
Hooray!

212
00:12:07,293 --> 00:12:09,820
As long as Boxo's with
me, I'm good! I get it.

213
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:11,157
In spooky situations,

214
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:14,257
it's way easier to handle it when
you've got somebody else by your side.

215
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:18,340
But I'm a vending machine, so, uh,
I'm not sure if this even counts.

216
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:22,560
Boxo, are you still there?
Say something! Hello there!

217
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:24,430
Thank goodness.

218
00:12:24,513 --> 00:12:26,640
Keep talking to me, okay? Hello there!

219
00:12:27,060 --> 00:12:28,557
And you better not fall off.

220
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:31,417
There's no way I could do
this without you by my side.

221
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:34,717
It's almost like she's a kid
learning how to ride a bike.

222
00:12:34,800 --> 00:12:36,260
I can't give up.

223
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:39,160
I swear, I'll do better.

224
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,957
Don't leave me.

225
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:44,720
I want us to keep on exploring together.

226
00:12:46,420 --> 00:12:47,400
I see.

227
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:50,097
Lamas is desperately
trying to overcome her

228
00:12:50,180 --> 00:12:52,709
fear so she and I can
stay with each other.

229
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,800
In that case, I'll help her any way I can.

230
00:12:58,580 --> 00:13:00,997
This device disperses
scents around the vending

231
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,217
machine in order to draw a customer's end.

232
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,780
Let's go ahead and try out a coffee aroma.

233
00:13:08,460 --> 00:13:09,560
What's going on?

234
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:11,380
Something smells good.

235
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:13,520
Now for step two.

236
00:13:18,580 --> 00:13:19,420
Oh, wow.

237
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:23,000
This music is making me feel
a whole lot calmer. Great.

238
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:24,888
It looks like it's working.

239
00:13:25,980 --> 00:13:27,940
I wonder if I'm doing too much.

240
00:13:30,900 --> 00:13:31,940
There you are.

241
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:33,397
Check it out, everyone.

242
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:35,068
I've got this down pat now.

243
00:13:35,460 --> 00:13:38,840
I'm not afraid anymore.
Good job. Nice one.

244
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:40,340
I knew you could do it.

245
00:13:40,540 --> 00:13:41,370
All right.

246
00:13:41,453 --> 00:13:43,277
Now it's time for you
to move on to step two.

247
00:13:43,360 --> 00:13:45,700
No matter what it is, I can handle it.

248
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:47,257
Look who's a pro now.

249
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:50,557
So you won't mind setting down
Boxo and going around again.

250
00:13:50,640 --> 00:13:51,470
Oh, thanks.

251
00:13:51,553 --> 00:13:52,737
I'm going to have to decline.

252
00:13:52,820 --> 00:13:54,857
She didn't even think twice about it.

253
00:13:54,940 --> 00:13:56,999
Her resolve is impressive in a way.

254
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,180
Ah, there you are.

255
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:02,717
I've come back with some hunters
to help with the campaign.

256
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,360
The band of gluttons, huh?

257
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:05,880
Nice to see you again.

258
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:07,700
And Mishuel.

259
00:14:08,100 --> 00:14:09,159
It's been a while.

260
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:11,980
Thanks so much for having us. Wow!

261
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,257
He actually reached out
to the Menagerie of Fools.

262
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:17,377
It'll be good to have
another strong fighter,

263
00:14:17,460 --> 00:14:21,297
but I wonder if he'll be able to
handle being in a group this big.

264
00:14:21,380 --> 00:14:24,077
Lichuel mentioned that he
went on an adventure with you.

265
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:26,177
We asked him to join
the Menagerie of Fools,

266
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:28,257
but he wanted to have
a trial period first.

267
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:32,037
This campaign will help him decide if
he wants to sign on for real, right?

268
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:35,457
I'd love to join, but I wanted
to make sure we'd be a good fit.

269
00:14:35,540 --> 00:14:38,257
I'd hate to accept and
become a burden on everyone.

270
00:14:38,340 --> 00:14:40,037
Let's see if I can handle teamwork.

271
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:43,217
It sounds like he's just
being modest, But knowing him,

272
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:46,418
that is something to be
legitimately concerned about.

273
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:47,617
Okay, to summarize,

274
00:14:47,700 --> 00:14:50,257
our primary objective
in coming to the Dead's

275
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:53,120
Lament Stratum is to
locate the Stratum Lord,

276
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:54,299
the King of Souls,

277
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:55,420
and take him out.

278
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:59,960
This won't be an easy job, but I'm
sure you can handle it no problem.

279
00:15:00,160 --> 00:15:01,477
I don't really get it myself,

280
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:03,477
but I hear humans have
lots of trouble dealing

281
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:05,777
with dark places and
stuff like corpse fiends.

282
00:15:05,860 --> 00:15:06,690
They do?

283
00:15:06,773 --> 00:15:07,758
That's interesting.

284
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:08,937
Well, I don't blame them.

285
00:15:09,020 --> 00:15:10,317
I hate corpse fiends too.

286
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,937
They smell like rotten meat.

287
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:14,844
Yep, one whiff and say
goodbye to your appetite.

288
00:15:14,960 --> 00:15:16,577
I've never thought about it before,

289
00:15:16,660 --> 00:15:19,660
but humans and beast people
see horror differently.

290
00:15:19,800 --> 00:15:22,597
Make sure you come back to
the inn before nightfall.

291
00:15:22,680 --> 00:15:24,445
Everyone, prepare to move out!

292
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:25,840
Yes, sir!

293
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:28,946
Lamas, what was that
crunching sound just now?

294
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:36,257
I don't get why they put their
graves outside the village.

295
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:38,037
Who knows why humans do anything?

296
00:15:38,120 --> 00:15:38,950
They're weird.

297
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,937
Mikenne, in short, don't know
what they're talking about.

298
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:43,397
It's for the heck of it.

299
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,310
I don't know,

300
00:15:44,393 --> 00:15:47,877
but if you left an offering on a
gravestone, monsters would just eat it.

301
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:48,790
What a waste.

302
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:50,840
Hang on a sec!

303
00:15:52,900 --> 00:15:54,724
I was afraid this would happen.

304
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,497
They're all around us.

305
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:02,580
You ready, Shiro?

306
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:04,680
I was born ready, Akka.

307
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:07,500
Just give us the word, Captain. Let's go.

308
00:16:15,420 --> 00:16:16,250
Amazing!

309
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:17,720
Look at them go!

310
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,412
They're destroying them!

311
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:24,457
Now that I've been here
for a couple of days,

312
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:29,097
I get the sense that the monsters are looking
into the windows with a sense of envy.

313
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:31,897
I've heard rumors that,
unlike typical monsters,

314
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:34,857
the ones in this stratum
are made from dead humans.

315
00:16:34,940 --> 00:16:36,293
Maybe it's really true.

316
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,112
Where did you come from?

317
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:40,700
Please insert coins.

318
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:42,300
Oh, come on!

319
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:46,462
Even in moments like this, I can
still only use my canned phrases?

320
00:16:49,940 --> 00:16:51,999
I don't think he means me any harm.

321
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:56,097
If I'm being honest, this kid
looks more curious than malicious.

322
00:16:56,180 --> 00:16:58,237
It would feel wrong to be mean to him.

323
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,150
Hello there!

324
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:01,510
Hmm?

325
00:17:01,740 --> 00:17:03,040
Whoa, uh, hold on.

326
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:04,460
Hey, cut it out.

327
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:07,057
Come on, kid, don't grab at me like that.

328
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:09,617
Listen, if you stop doing that,
I'll give you one of these.

329
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:10,530
Sound good?

330
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:19,080
All right, drink up. Go on.

331
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:40,793
Well, well, looks like it's another
busy night for the loitering monsters.

332
00:17:43,320 --> 00:17:44,860
Is that the same kid?

333
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,160
In that case.

334
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:55,675
I wonder why he came back to me again.

335
00:17:56,100 --> 00:17:57,806
Does he like me or something?

336
00:17:58,420 --> 00:18:00,949
He's probably just a
kid expecting a treat.

337
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:03,205
Night after night, he came by.

338
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:05,557
I never expected to say this,

339
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:09,758
but I actually started to look forward
to our late-night interactions.

340
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:12,657
Things have been going well,

341
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:16,740
so this is the first time we've
decided to camp outside the village.

342
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:21,640
I guess I can't give that corpse
fiend child any orange juice today.

343
00:18:22,140 --> 00:18:26,022
Well, we're going back tomorrow,
so he's only going to miss a day.

344
00:18:27,960 --> 00:18:28,977
A corpse fiend.

345
00:18:29,060 --> 00:18:32,413
There's just one, but it looks
like it's headed this way.

346
00:18:34,500 --> 00:18:35,980
Aka, what should we do?

347
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:38,572
If it's alone, we can take it out, Shiro.

348
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:39,890
Right.

349
00:18:39,973 --> 00:18:41,135
I'll do my part, too.

350
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,840
Is that him? A child, huh?

351
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:51,257
I feel bad, but...

352
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:53,580
Rest in peace, kid! You best!

353
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,720
Is something wrong, Boxo?

354
00:19:02,820 --> 00:19:04,117
What's with all the shouting?

355
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:06,677
That corpse fiend he killed. No way.

356
00:19:06,760 --> 00:19:08,231
Could it be the same one?

357
00:19:08,740 --> 00:19:09,600
Huh? Wait.

358
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:12,317
Isn't this a label from
one of your drinks?

359
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:14,457
Why would a monster carry this around?

360
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:17,246
I know I shouldn't blame
Akka for what he did.

361
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,600
It's not his fault.

362
00:19:19,800 --> 00:19:22,094
But I feel like I'm about to short out.

363
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:24,800
He dropped a copper coin.

364
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:27,257
Don't tell me he was
trying to buy something.

365
00:19:27,340 --> 00:19:29,164
There's no way that's possible.

366
00:19:29,320 --> 00:19:31,657
I don't know if it was
the same corpse fiend,

367
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:34,697
but there was one that was
watching us from a distance.

368
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:37,427
It didn't try anything,
so I just ignored it.

369
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:39,280
Ah, I see now.

370
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:44,228
He was going to try to put that coin in
me because he saw others buying items.

371
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:47,200
How silly.

372
00:19:47,940 --> 00:19:50,517
Children don't need to
worry about stuff like that.

373
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:53,247
Besides, all he had was
a single copper coin.

374
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,660
That's not enough to buy anything.

375
00:19:56,380 --> 00:19:57,800
Please insert coins.

376
00:20:01,900 --> 00:20:03,320
You want the usual, huh?

377
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:09,090
Good job!

378
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,660
You all did well.

379
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:14,313
We now have an idea of where
the King of Souls is hiding.

380
00:20:14,540 --> 00:20:15,952
So what's our next move?

381
00:20:16,060 --> 00:20:18,217
I'm sure you've thought of
some way to deal with him.

382
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:19,130
Maybe.

383
00:20:19,213 --> 00:20:21,717
I actually wanted to compare
notes with you first.

384
00:20:21,800 --> 00:20:24,297
Do you know what kind of
monster the King of Souls is?

385
00:20:24,380 --> 00:20:28,909
Not sure, but according to the rumors,
he's some sort of powerful magic user.

386
00:20:29,260 --> 00:20:30,789
Yeah, I've heard that too.

387
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:35,017
He's got a ton of magic power and uses
lots of different elemental spells.

388
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:36,924
Not a great combination for us.

389
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:39,337
Got any thoughts on how
to deal with his magic?

390
00:20:39,420 --> 00:20:40,420
Here's the thing.

391
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:44,997
Don't we have somebody in our party with
the ability to block any kind of attack?

392
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:47,727
Wait, you're not talking
about Boxo, are you?

393
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:49,300
Ding, ding, you got it.

394
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:53,737
His barrier can block pretty much anything
you throw at it, including magic spells.

395
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:56,797
If you rush in with Boxo, you
don't even have to take him down.

396
00:20:56,880 --> 00:21:00,233
Just keeping the King of Souls
distracted is good enough.

397
00:21:00,400 --> 00:21:02,580
Ah, so that's how it is.

398
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:06,737
I'm guessing this is the real reason he
was so insistent on bringing me along.

399
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:07,650
That's true.

400
00:21:07,880 --> 00:21:11,837
I remember that he was able to block
spells back in the Labyrinth Stratum.

401
00:21:11,920 --> 00:21:12,957
What do you think?

402
00:21:13,040 --> 00:21:16,517
I'll come up with a new plan from
scratch if you're not confident.

403
00:21:16,600 --> 00:21:18,460
Your call. Hello there!

404
00:21:18,760 --> 00:21:21,097
I knew I could count on
you, my Boxxo friend.

405
00:21:21,180 --> 00:21:22,062
You're the man.

406
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:24,797
As long as he's okay with
it, I'm on board too.

407
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:25,900
That settles it.

408
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:27,597
As his name suggests,

409
00:21:27,680 --> 00:21:31,517
the King of Souls has a number of other
monsters serving as his bodyguards.

410
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:33,297
You can ignore the small fry.

411
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:34,437
We'll take care of them.

412
00:21:34,520 --> 00:21:35,350
Sure.

413
00:21:35,433 --> 00:21:38,160
Don't get too worked up
now, Lamas. Yeah, I know.

414
00:21:38,520 --> 00:21:42,017
Everyone here has come together
to work towards the same goal.

415
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:43,157
We've agreed on a plan,

416
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:46,157
and so the rest depends on what
happens when we face our foe.

417
00:21:46,240 --> 00:21:48,652
For now, let's drink to lift our spirits.

418
00:21:49,140 --> 00:21:50,020
Box up!

419
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:54,997
Boxo, thank you.

420
00:21:55,080 --> 00:21:56,380
Hello there!

421
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,577
Once we finish up with this quest,

422
00:21:59,660 --> 00:22:02,719
I wouldn't mind having
another toast with everybody!

423
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:28,139
I hope you can see that the
smile is waiting for me.

424
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:32,957
It's impossible to see,
but it's a special day!

425
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:35,477
I would like to be a good day.

426
00:22:35,560 --> 00:22:38,097
I want to make a dream.

427
00:22:38,180 --> 00:22:39,997
I want to make a dream.

428
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:41,551
I want to see the future.

429
00:22:41,820 --> 00:22:46,157
I don't know who knows,
but it's not the moment.

430
00:22:46,240 --> 00:22:50,197
I'll be happy with this moment.

431
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:52,377
Today's day is a good day.

432
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:53,877
Thank

433
00:22:53,960 --> 00:23:00,900
you.
